From: Camera Firmware Integration <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: avoid intermediate metadata and error copies

Borrow frame metadata only within synchronous preprocessing; retain the owned
metadata snapshot captured by the asynchronous completion callback. Lock the
request requeue weak pointer without an extra weak-reference copy.

Borrow errors from owned Results and allow local Results to move on return.
Retain error snapshots across cleanup/recovery callbacks that may mutate
borrowed static-lifetime errors; add regressions for startup and promotion
failure. Preserve validation, rollback and callback lifetime semantics.
No public API, authentication policy or database format changes.

Upstream-Status: Pending

